  "description": "Captures a relationship being re-authored in real time. A writer and a gallery owner drive through Tuscany discussing copies and originals; somewhere in the afternoon, without a cut you can point to, they begin performing fifteen years of marriage. You cannot locate the edit where strangers became spouses — the film is a controlled experiment in how little evidence an observer needs.\n\nIn Tuscany to promote his latest book, a middle-aged British writer meets a French woman who leads him to the village of Lucignano. While there, a chance question reveals something deeper.",
